        <h3>Where May 1 Fell in Each Run</h3>
        <p>The weeks split three ways:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>{{N_FIRST}} songs were in their first week at number one: "ABC," "(Hey Won't You Play) Another Somebody Done Somebody Wrong Song," "Let Your Love Flow," "Southern Nights" and "Heart of Glass."</li>
          <li>"ABC" was the only one of those that stayed on top for a second week.</li>
          <li>{{N_MID}} were in the middle of a longer run: "Joy to the World," "The First Time Ever I Saw Your Face," "Tie a Yellow Ribbon Round the Ole Oak Tree" and "Night Fever."</li>
          <li>{{N_LAST}} was in the last week of its run: "TSOP (The Sound of Philadelphia)."</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Test Your Own Memory</h3>
        <p>Which of these ten May 1 in music history number ones would you have bet on?</p>
        <p>The list runs from The Jackson 5 in 1970 to Blondie in 1979.</p>
        <p>Other weeks have their own lists, including <a href="/blog/trivia/october-8-in-music-history/">October 8 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/february-1-in-music-history/">February 1 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/december-12-in-music-history/">December 12 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/november-7-in-music-history/">November 7 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/september-16-in-music-history/">September 16 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/august-19-in-music-history/">August 19 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/july-15-in-music-history/">July 15 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/june-12-in-music-history/">June 12 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/may-29-in-music-history/">May 29 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/february-13-in-music-history/">February 13 in music history</a>, <a href="/blog/trivia/january-9-in-music-history/">January 9 in music history</a> and <a href="/blog/trivia/november-28-in-music-history/">November 28 in music history</a>.</p>
        <p>The <a href="/pages/70s-trivia-quiz">70s Music Trivia Quiz</a> has ten new questions each round.</p>
        <p>For the whole decade at the top, see the <a href="/blog/songs/70s-number-one-hits/">70s number one hits</a> page.</p>
        <p>More of the decade lives on the <a href="/">Music of the 70s</a> home page.</p>

